  "analysis": [
    {
      "label": "Context",
      "text": "Brazil led 3–1 with minutes left, so Italy had to push forward. The gaps that opened behind the Italian midfield gave Brazil room to keep the ball and build patiently from deep."
    },
    {
      "label": "Build-up",
      "text": "Clodoaldo's dribble in the Brazil half pulled Italians towards the ball. Rivellino then switched the point of attack down the left, where Jairzinho was waiting."
    },
    {
      "label": "Key moment",
      "text": "Jairzinho drifted inside from the left and Facchetti followed. By tracking the winger man-to-man, the full-back left Italy's left flank empty, exactly the lane Carlos Alberto was running into."
    },
    {
      "label": "The finish",
      "text": "Pelé held the ball at the edge of the box to draw the defence, then rolled it into the captain's stride. Carlos Alberto struck first time, low and hard, before Albertosi could set."
    }
